  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "How Your Local AI Stack Is an Act of Sovereignty*",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "I. The Canvas Is Code",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "That moment, for the AI practitioner, is the moment you stop renting intelligence and start building the machinery that thinks on your behalf",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "agentic knowledge graphs, writing frameworks that route, reason, and respond without sending a single token to a server I don't control. What I've come to understand — slowly, then all at once — is that the *choice* of how you build is not a technical decision",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Your AI architecture is not infrastructure",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": ", and somewhere in a data center you will never visit, a model you cannot inspect processes your most private questions using weights you did not choose, governed by policies you did not write. This is the default",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The question I want to ask in this post is not \"which AI should I use",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "That's the consumer's question. The question I want to ask is : *what does it mean to own your execution path",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "That shift is sovereignty",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "And the stack you build is its expression",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "s AI Act and the wave of state-level legislation following it — gesture toward accountability, but they're fundamentally reactive. They tell you what happened after the consequential action. They are , at best, sophisticated telemetry",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The \"Reasonable Care\" standard that anchors most enterprise AI governance is a legal fiction when you don't control the boundary",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Think about what it means to be a writer feeding your unfinished work into a model you cannot audit",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Every one of these is an act of creative surrender disguised as productivity",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "across many posts on this site — from the [inference geography piece](https://danielkliewer.com/blog/2025-11-14-2025-inference-new-geography-intelligence) that looked at how *where* compute runs is becoming a geopolitical question, to the [llama",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": ".com/blog/2025-11-12-mastering-llama-cpp-local-llm-integration-guide) that gave a ground-level view of what local execution actually looks like in production. The throughline across all of it is the same: **who controls the execution path controls the output**",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "And right now, for most people, the answer is not them",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The cultural cost of this arrangement is hard to quantify but easy to feel",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "A Mixture of Experts system — MoE, in the literature — is , at its simplest, a system that dynamically routes queries to specialized sub-models",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not new as a concept in machine learning. What's new is the possibility of *you* building one",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The router is the first thing a query touches",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Its job is interpretation: what kind of problem is this",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "/2025-03-13-simulacra), which integrates the OpenAI Agents SDK with Ollama for locally-hosted agents, the routing logic lives in a handoff layer that evaluates intent before dispatching. The router is not passive — it's the system's first act of interpretation",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "When you build this yourself, every routing rule you write is a decision about what *you* value",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Each expert in the pool is a model — or a model configuration — specialized for a domain",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
  ],
